The Security Council,

Bearing in mind the Treaty on Principles Governing the Activities of States in the Exploration and Use of Outer Space, including the Moon and Other Celestial Bodies, in particular article IV thereof,

Affirming that outer space is a global commons where the interests of all countries are intertwined with a common stake, and that the exploration and use of outer space shall be carried out for the benefit and in the interests of all countries and shall be the province of all mankind,

Recalling the Treaty on the Non-Proliferation of Nuclear Weapons,

Recalling its primary responsibility under the Charter of the United Nations for the maintenance of international peace and security,

Recognizing that the prevention of an arms race in outer space would avert a grave danger for international peace and security,

Recognizing also that the prevention of the weaponization of outer space and of an arms race in outer space represents the common aspiration and urgent demand of the international community,

Emphasizing the importance of strict compliance with existing legal regimes on outer space, and reaffirming the need for further measures, including commitments to prevent the placement of weapons of any kind in outer space,

1. Calls upon all States, in particular those with major space capabilities:
(a) To contribute actively to the objective of the peaceful use of outer space and of the prevention of an arms race in outer space;
(b) To refrain from actions contrary to that objective and to the relevant existing treaties in the interest of maintaining international peace and security and promoting international cooperation;
(c) To take urgent measures to prevent for all time the placement of weapons in outer space and the threat or use of force in outer space, from space against Earth and from Earth against objects in outer space;

2. Calls upon all States parties to the Treaty on Principles Governing the Activities of States in the Exploration and Use of Outer Space, including the Moon and Other Celestial Bodies, to comply fully with their obligations under that Treaty, including not to place in orbit around the Earth any objects carrying nuclear weapons or any other kinds of weapons of mass destruction, install such weapons on celestial bodies, or station such weapons in outer space in any other manner;

3. Calls on all Member States to actively support the objective of the peaceful use of outer space and to prevent the placement of weapons of any kind in outer space;

4. Emphasizes the necessity of further measures, including the early commencement of negotiations on an international legally binding instrument on the prevention of an arms race in outer space in all its aspects, taking into account the draft treaty on the prevention of the placement of weapons in outer space, the threat or use of force against outer space objects;

5. Reaffirms the primary role of the Conference on Disarmament as the single multilateral disarmament negotiating forum, and urges the Conference on Disarmament to agree on and implement at its earliest opportunity a balanced and comprehensive programme of work, including the immediate commencement of negotiations on an international legally binding instrument on the prevention of an arms race in outer space in all its aspects.

